From 07ff476766d2bb2d3bb873323454e7354e52e229 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:30:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Replace libguestfs.keyring with the current key at
https://download.libguestfs.org/rich@annexia.org-pubkey.txt. That file
holds only F7774FB1AD074A7E8C8767EA91738F73E1B768A0; the other
certificate(s) in the keyring (2B7C1A53420D4AF3BFF4738BF382AE19F4850180,
71C2CC22B1C4602927D2F3AAA7A16B4A2527436A,
BC2BFC18CF52DEA925F51215C9A12EDF2527436A) are dropped.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 libguestfs.keyring | Bin 82814 -> 4004 bytes
 libnbd.spec        |   2 ++
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

